  "description": "Summarise an epic or a pull request for someone not in the conversation that produced it: what the work is and for whom, why now, scope, what it touches and where in the code, who decides, unfamiliar terms, and where it is easy to go wrong. For an epic, also the understanding check the developer answers before coding. Use when a person joins work in flight, picks up an epic they did not write, or reviews a pull request in an unfamiliar area; what merged work now does is `atk:spec`. Also explains in plain words, finding by finding or section by section, a document a person was handed, a record the kit wrote or any other, such as a vendor's penetration test report; turning one into requirements is `atk:intake`. Triggers on: \"catchup\", \"summarize issue\", \"summarize PR\", \"explain this document\", \"explain these findings simply\", \"/atk:catchup\".",
